# Build context exclusions for cloud/web-server/deploy.sh.
#
# Why a separate file: the web-server image does NOT need anything in
# web-next/. Excluding it shrinks the upload by ~150 MiB AND avoids the
# 2026-05-11 race where a parallel web-next deploy was rewriting
# web-next/.next/ while web-server's tarball walk hit
# `web-next/.next/images-manifest.json` mid-rebuild → FileNotFoundError
# from gcloud's archive step.
#
# Strategy: include the root .gcloudignore patterns (mirror of .gitignore
# + cloud-specific) AND add web-next/ on top. The .gcloudignore syntax
# (gsutil-style) doesn't support !include, so we duplicate the contents
# rather than diverge. Keep the duplicated section in sync if the root
# file changes.

# === From .gcloudignore (keep in sync) ===

# Python / venvs
.venv/
.venv-*/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Env / secrets
.env
.agent-token

# OS / IDE
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
.git/

# Build artifacts
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/
dist/
build/

# Model weights
*.onnx
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.ckpt

# Heavy regenerable per-channel dirs
**/footage/
**/cache/
**/scratch/
**/emoji/
**/tts_tests/
**/cooking_loops/
**/critiques/

# === Cloud-web-server-only additions ===

# The FastAPI image's Dockerfile only COPYs web/, pipeline/, control/,
# requirements-control.txt and a tiny channel-assets subdir. web-next/
# (the Next.js build output) is unrelated and ~150 MiB. Exclude wholesale.
web-next/
